  "notes": "TenantKeep: one registration that TenantKeep Posture and TenantKeep On-Call both sign in to for everything they read. Public client, no credentials, and it exposes nothing. Every permission on it is read-only by its name, on every API: a refresh token for a registration can be redeemed for any API a tenant granted it, so one broader permission anywhere would make that untrue. resources is what Posture asks for: the Graph reads, and Power BI's Tenant.Read.All, which is optional and approved from a link of its own. sharedWith is what On-Call asks for, by name, when a customer approves it from On-Call's own link; Posture never requests those. The APIs that have no read-only permission at all (Azure Service Management, the Teams admin API, the Power Platform admin API) are read through a second registration, app-services.json. Nothing that writes is here: every write lives in a separate On-Call app, and SharePoint full control lives only in the optional app-sharepoint.json, granted to named admins. Owned by Kainor LLC; the manifest is published in the Posture source repository.",
  "resources": [
    {
